<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.5 </span>Image Editing</h3>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report image editing performance on the Image-Edit Bench in Table <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 4.5 Image Editing ‣ 4 Experiment ‣ Lavida-O: Elastic Masked Diffusion Models for Unified Multimodal Understanding and Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. Lavida-O outperforms state-of-the-art unified models such as BAGEL and specialized models like FluxKontext-dev. Most notably, Lavida-O even outperforms the state-of-the-art closed-sourced model GPT4-o<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI, 2024</a>)</cite> on replacing and removing objects, which requires localized understanding of the image. This underscores the effectiveness of Lavida-O’s design in integrating object grounding capabilities.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="S4.T5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Quantative results on Image-Edit benchmark.<span id="S4.T5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We report the per-category and overall score on Image-Edit Benchmark.</span></span></figcaption>
<div id="S4.T5.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:82.8pt;vertical-align:-40.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-254.9pt,61.2pt) scale(0.403570928153947,0.403570928153947) ;">
<table id="S4.T5.6.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
